{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Dyson Signal","logline":"When an old skybridge relay picks up a signal from a distant Dyson swarm, cartographer Veya and Cartel toll-master Kael clash over whether the isles should answer it, while the Cartel's grip on trade and a crumbling bridge network threaten to turn a moment of wonder into ruin.","theme":"Some truths are safer shared than hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Relay Wakes","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_relay_hums","title":"The Relay Hums","summary":"While charting fading skybridges, Veya notices a strange, patterned pulse from an old relay on the Silverspine bridge network. Her wind-sight shows the currents bending around it in ways no storm has ever caused.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Chart the failing bridge near the old relay and find out why the wind currents around it have shifted.","conflict":"Veya's late mentor's theory is unproven, the Academy dismisses relay anomalies, and her stubbornness makes her work alone rather than ask for help.","outcome":"Veya records a repeating signal that is clearly structured and clearly not from the isles, and decides to keep it secret until she is sure."},{"id":"scn_swarm_decoded","title":"A Swarm Beyond the Sky","summary":"Working through the night in the Academy's chart rooms, Veya matches the signal's rhythm to her mentor's notes on the drift. She concludes it comes from a vast ring of machines circling a distant sun, a Dyson swarm, and that it may be a greeting.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Decode enough of the signal to prove it is a message and not natural noise.","conflict":"Her mentor's notes are incomplete, and her flaw pushes her to keep refining the result instead of admitting she needs more people to confirm it.","outcome":"She has a draft interpretation that suggests the swarm wants an answer, and she realises answering would need a relay powerful enough to reach it.","depends_on":["scn_relay_hums"]},{"id":"scn_ledger_whisper","title":"A Whisper in the Ledgers","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael's ledger-mastery picks up a spike in bridge-wardens' requests for relay parts and an unusual flow of Academy chart orders. He deduces that Veya has found something valuable.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Find out what Silverspine is quietly buying and why before the Cartel's rivals learn of it.","conflict":"The Wardens accuse him of sabotaging forge-island supplies, so every inquiry he makes looks like interference, and his admiration for Veya makes him hesitate.","outcome":"Kael concludes that whoever controls the signal controls the last stable routes, and sends word asking Veya to meet him."}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Who Answers the Sky","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_rivals_meet","title":"Old Apprentices, New Terms","summary":"Veya and Kael meet at Mistral Docks. Kael offers to fund a powerful transmitter in exchange for exclusive rights to her charts and to any reply. She refuses, and neither will concede.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to learn what Kael knows without revealing her decoding; Kael wants her charts and the signal under Cartel control.","conflict":"Their shared past, her refusal to let him control her work, and his belief that everything has a price collide in open rivalry.","outcome":"Veya leaves convinced the Cartel will bury or seize her work, and Kael quietly orders enforcers to watch her.","depends_on":["scn_swarm_decoded","scn_ledger_whisper"]},{"id":"scn_secret_paths","title":"The Hollow's Secret Paths","summary":"Pursued by Cartel agents, Veya flees to The Hollow where Maris hides her in the service corridors between windmills and granaries. They trade wind-current knowledge for Maris's unmapped paths.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya needs a safe hiding place and a way to reach the Emberroost forges without using Cartel-watched bridges; Maris wants to keep her smuggling routes safe.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and fears that sheltering Veya will draw enforcers to the grain smuggling the isle depends on, while the grain levy is already tightening.","outcome":"Maris agrees to guide Veya through her corridors, and Veya shares enough of the signal to earn her trust.","depends_on":["scn_rivals_meet"]},{"id":"scn_forge_cables","title":"Cables at Emberroost","summary":"Guided by Maris, Veya reaches Emberroost and asks the Bridge Wardens for a relay strong enough to answer the swarm. The Wardens warn that the failing bridges and the rule against open flame limit what can be built.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Persuade the Wardens to braid a transmitter cable from cloudstone and fit it to the old relay.","conflict":"Supplies are short because of suspected Cartel sabotage, the build must be done inside shielded forge-pits, and Veya cannot admit her decoding still has gaps.","outcome":"The Wardens agree to build the cable, but only if Veya's charts are shared openly with them, forcing her first step toward sharing.","depends_on":["scn_secret_paths"]},{"id":"scn_sabotage_proof","title":"The Broken Shipment","summary":"Kael arrives at Emberroost with Cartel enforcers claiming the right to inspect all relay parts. Veya and the Wardens expose a sabotaged cloudstone shipment, and Kael has to decide whether to defend or disown it.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants proof of sabotage to protect the build; Kael wants to take control of the cable and the charts.","conflict":"Kael's pragmatism and his belief that price equals worth collide with the evidence, and Maris's smuggling routes are exposed to the enforcers.","outcome":"The enforcers seize the unfinished cable and arrest Maris's contacts, Kael takes the charts, and Veya is forced to admit she was wrong to distrust the Wardens.","depends_on":["scn_forge_cables"]},{"id":"scn_charts_shared","title":"Truth Shared at Silverspine","summary":"Veya returns to Silverspine and shows her full signal data and bridge charts to the scholars, admitting her errors. The Academy confirms the decoding and spreads it to the isles, so the Cartel can no longer bury it.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Make the signal public so no single faction can own it.","conflict":"Veya's pride resists admitting mistakes in front of her peers, and Maris questions whether giving up the secret will leave her isle exposed.","outcome":"The isles now know of the Dyson swarm, the Cartel loses its secrecy advantage, and the Bridge Wardens demand the cable back.","depends_on":["scn_sabotage_proof"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Answer","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_relay_standoff","title":"Standoff at the Relay","summary":"At the old relay, the Wardens, the Cartel and the Hollow Circle gather. Kael holds the cable and the lanes, Veya holds the decoded signal, and the bridge begins to fail beneath them.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants the relay answered openly; Kael wants the last stable routes and the transmission under Cartel control.","conflict":"The bridge is breaking, Kael's monopoly would fail if the answer were shared, and Veya must trust a rival she cannot forgive.","outcome":"Maris leads the crowd to safety through her corridors, and Kael sees that control will cost more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_charts_shared","scn_sabotage_proof"]},{"id":"scn_choice_to_answer","title":"The Choice to Answer","summary":"Using her wind-sight, Veya charts a safe route while Kael's ledger-mastery brokers a shared agreement among the factions. The Cartel hands over the cable, the Wardens fit it, and the isles send their reply together.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Join the factions in sending one answer to the swarm and stabilise the bridge.","conflict":"Wind-debt, toll grievances and distrust threaten to break the agreement, and Veya and Kael each have to give up what they most wanted.","outcome":"The answer is transmitted and the bridge holds, and a reply pulse begins to travel back from the swarm.","depends_on":["scn_relay_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"After the Reply","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_new_charter","title":"Tolls Rewritten","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael presents a revised toll arrangement with the Wardens that eases the wind-debt on essential crossings and lifts the grain levy on The Hollow. The merchants are stunned that he chose it.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to rebuild the Cartel's standing on terms the isles will accept.","conflict":"Cartel princes object to the loss of revenue, and Kael has to weigh price against worth for the first time.","outcome":"The agreement passes narrowly, ending the worst of the Toll War and easing the grain levy.","depends_on":["scn_choice_to_answer"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"A Quiet Harvest","summary":"Back in The Hollow, Maris watches grain move openly along the mended bridges. She forgives Kael only partly, and accepts that her quiet work helped save the isles as much as any open stand.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants to see The Hollow fed without smuggling, and to settle her friendship with Veya.","conflict":"Her slow trust and reluctance to forgive make her doubt that the peace will last.","outcome":"Maris puts away her smuggling routes and keeps her friendship with Veya, which now rests on shared trust.","depends_on":["scn_new_charter"]},{"id":"scn_new_charts","title":"Charts for Everyone","summary":"Veya publishes the full chart of the bridges and the swarm's reply at Silverspine, crediting the Wardens, Maris and her mentor. She sends a copy to Kael, who accepts it as an equal.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to share the charts and the reply openly, and to finish her mentor's work.","conflict":"She still struggles to admit her mistakes in public, and the reply from the swarm raises questions the isles cannot yet answer.","outcome":"The isles face the swarm's reply together, with open charts, easier tolls and a new willingness to share what they know.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest"]}]}]}
</Output>
