ya is tested before the whole dock.","outcome":"The payment falls short by a single crossing, and Kael prepares to close the bridge.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_betrayal_choice","scn_veya_admits"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_crossing","title":"The Shared Crossing","summary":"Veya publishes her charts openly, so every crossing is counted and shared among the Wardens, the Circle and the merchants. Maris guides the cargo through service corridors while Kael weighs whether controlling the bridge is worth its collapse.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to complete the final crossing and clear the debt, and Kael wants to stop them.","conflict":"The span begins to fail in the wind, and Kael must choose between sabotaging the crossing and saving the bridge his monopoly depends on.","outcome":"Kael lets the crossing proceed and the debt is cleared, and the bridge holds.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Wind Left","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_reckoning","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"Kael faces the Cartel after losing the debt and the routes. He reckons that control cost more than it gained and chooses to open the ledgers to the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to face the consequences of his failure and Veya wants to finish the shared chart.","conflict":"Kael's belief that price equals worth clashes with the worth he saw in Veya's open charts.","outcome":"Kael agrees to a fairer toll arrangement and shares his ledgers on the sabotage, easing the Toll War.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_return","title":"The Hollow Fed","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow with the grain levy eased and the silos refilled. She accepts that quiet hiding and open standing are both forms of courage.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to see her isle fed and to repair her friendship with Veya.","conflict":"Her habit of distrust makes it hard to forgive Veya, even after Veya's apology.","outcome":"Maris keeps the secret corridors for her isle and forgives Veya, sealing their alliance.","depends_on":["scn_kael_reckoning"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya posts the shared charts in the academy and the Wardens begin to reinforce the failing bridges. She starts to prove her mentor's theory with the whole archipelago's help.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to complete her mentor's work and have the charts kept open for all.","conflict":"Some scholars want recognition for Veya alone, tempting her toward the ambition she fears.","outcome":"Veya credits Maris and the Wardens, learning that shared truths keep the bridges standing.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_return"]}]}]}
