{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Wind Debt Run","logline":"When a band of smugglers owes an impossible wind-debt that must be repaid before the season turns, cartographer Veya and miller's daughter Maris must outmaneuver toll-master Kael or lose the last stable skybridge that keeps their isles alive.","theme":"Some burdens are lighter when shared than when hoarded","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Debt Comes Due","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_shortfall","title":"The Empty Silos","summary":"Maris shows the Hollow Circle that the grain levy and a season of bridge crossings have left a wind-debt far larger than the isle can repay, and that the last bridge to the archipelago will be closed if it goes unpaid.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to find a way to keep The Hollow fed and keep the last bridge open.","conflict":"The Cartel levy and the accrued wind-debt exceed anything the Hollow Circle can pay in labour or goods within the season.","outcome":"Maris resolves to smuggle grain along unmapped corridors and to seek a cartographer who can find a safe route."},{"id":"scn_veya_charts","title":"Charts That Must Be Buried","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya's wind-sight reveals that the skybridges are breaking faster than anyone admits, and that the last stable route is the one the Hollow's debt threatens to close. She refuses to hand her charts to a Cartel agent.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to chart a safe route through the breaking skybridge network and prove her mentor's theory.","conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants her charts buried, and her stubbornness keeps her from asking anyone for help.","outcome":"Veya decides to travel to Mistral Docks, where traders know which routes still hold.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_shortfall"]},{"id":"scn_kael_ledger","title":"The Toll-Master's Ledger","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael studies the Hollow's debt and sees it as a chance to seize the last stable skybridge routes before the bridges collapse. Veya arrives and the two old apprentices face each other across his ledger.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to turn the wind-debt into leverage over the last stable routes and to obtain Veya's charts.","conflict":"Veya will not let him control her charts, yet Kael's admiration for her skill makes him offer her a generous bargain he cannot afford to keep.","outcome":"Veya refuses, and Kael sets the Hollow's debt deadline to the turn of the season, with enforcers watching Maris's routes."},{"id":"scn_alliance_forged","title":"Secret Paths for Wind-Sight","summary":"Maris meets Veya at Mistral Docks and the two agree to trade knowledge: Veya's reading of wind currents for Maris's service corridors between granaries and windmills.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris and Veya want to form a partnership to move grain safely and map a route that can carry it.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly and suspects a Wardens-aligned cartographer of using her, while Veya cannot admit her charts are incomplete.","outcome":"They reach a cautious alliance and plan a run to Emberroost to secure cloudstone cable for the failing bridge.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_shortfall","scn_veya_charts","scn_kael_ledger"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Against the Season","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_cable","title":"Cable from the Forge","summary":"At Emberroost, Veya and Maris approach the Bridge Wardens for braided cloudstone cable, which can be paid for with labour against the wind-debt. The Wardens accuse Kael of sabotaging their supplies and demand proof of the Cartel's interference.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to obtain cloudstone cable and Warden labour credit to offset the debt.","conflict":"Supplies have been sabotaged and the Wardens distrust anyone carrying Cartel-marked goods, so Maris must hide her smuggled grain while Veya's pride makes her argue instead of negotiate.","outcome":"The Wardens grant a limited cable allotment in exchange for forge labour, and the pair learn that Kael's agents have been diverting supplies."},{"id":"scn_flame_near_miss","title":"A Spark Aloft","summary":"While hauling cable between isles, a Cartel enforcer's careless lantern nearly severs the bridge, in violation of the rule against open flame. Maris's pathfinding gets the cargo through a service corridor while Veya reads the wind to steady the cable.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to get the cable to the failing span without losing it or the bridge.","conflict":"Cartel enforcers close in on Maris's routes and the open flame threatens the cloudstone, forcing the pair to rely on each other's abilities.","outcome":"They save the cable but expose Maris's route to the Cartel, and the enforcer's flame becomes evidence of Kael's recklessness.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cable"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_error","title":"The Chart Was Wrong","summary":"Back at Silverspine, Veya's route fails when a span drifts out of place. She cannot admit the error and blames Maris's corridor, fracturing their alliance just as Kael's offer arrives.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to confirm her route and Kael wants to buy her charts while she is vulnerable.","conflict":"Veya's flaw leads her to blame Maris, and Maris's slow trust and unforgiving nature turn the quarrel into a break.","outcome":"Maris leaves for The Hollow and Veya is left alone with Kael's offer on the table.","depends_on":["scn_flame_near_miss"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_betrayal_choice","title":"Home or Friend","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow and finds the Cartel levy collectors at the silos. She must choose between the safe path of obeying the levy and the risk of continuing the run with Veya.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris wants to protect her isle's grain and Kael wants to claim the Hollow's debt guarantee.","conflict":"Kael charms and pressures her, offering to cancel part of the levy if she gives up the smuggling routes and Veya's location.","outcome":"Maris refuses to betray Veya, hides the grain instead, and sends word that she will meet Veya at the weakest bridge.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_error","scn_flame_near_miss"]},{"id":"scn_veya_admits","title":"Admitting the Error","summary":"Veya reviews the failed span and, with wind-sight, understands her chart was flawed. She decides to share the corrected charts with the Hollow Circle and the Wardens rather than sell or hoard them.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Veya wants to correct her chart and rebuild trust with Maris.","conflict":"Her pride and her fear of becoming like the Cartel leaders war against the need to admit she was wrong and share her work.","outcome":"She copies the charts for the Wardens and the Hollow, and sets out to meet Maris.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_error","scn_hollow_betrayal_choice"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Bridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_bridge_standoff","title":"Standoff on the Last Bridge","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael prepares to close the last stable bridge over the unpaid debt. Veya and Maris arrive with the corrected charts, the Wardens' cable and the Hollow's grain.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to repay the wind-debt in grain and labour before the season turns, and Kael wants to seize the route.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery finds the weakest point in their payment, a shortfall in labour, and Maris's trust in Veya is tested before the whole dock.","outcome":"The payment falls short by a single crossing, and Kael prepares to close the bridge.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_betrayal_choice","scn_veya_admits"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_crossing","title":"The Shared Crossing","summary":"Veya publishes her charts openly, so every crossing is counted and shared among the Wardens, the Circle and the merchants. Maris guides the cargo through service corridors while Kael weighs whether controlling the bridge is worth its collapse.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya and Maris want to complete the final crossing and clear the debt, and Kael wants to stop them.","conflict":"The span begins to fail in the wind, and Kael must choose between sabotaging the crossing and saving the bridge his monopoly depends on.","outcome":"Kael lets the crossing proceed and the debt is cleared, and the bridge holds.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_standoff"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"What the Wind Left","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_reckoning","title":"The Cost of Control","summary":"Kael faces the Cartel after losing the debt and the routes. He reckons that control cost more than it gained and chooses to open the ledgers to the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael wants to face the consequences of his failure and Veya wants to finish the shared chart.","conflict":"Kael's belief that price equals worth clashes with the worth he saw in Veya's open charts.","outcome":"Kael agrees to a fairer toll arrangement and shares his ledgers on the sabotage, easing the Toll War.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_return","title":"The Hollow Fed","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow with the grain levy eased and the silos refilled. She accepts that quiet hiding and open standing are both forms of courage.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Maris wants to see her isle fed and to repair her friendship with Veya.","conflict":"Her habit of distrust makes it hard to forgive Veya, even after Veya's apology.","outcome":"Maris keeps the secret corridors for her isle and forgives Veya, sealing their alliance.","depends_on":["scn_kael_reckoning"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_charts","title":"Charts Shared","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya posts the shared charts in the academy and the Wardens begin to reinforce the failing bridges. She starts to prove her mentor's theory with the whole archipelago's help.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to complete her mentor's work and have the charts kept open for all.","conflict":"Some scholars want recognition for Veya alone, tempting her toward the ambition she fears.","outcome":"Veya credits Maris and the Wardens, learning that shared truths keep the bridges standing.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_return"]}]}]}
