r_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants an unmapped route for her chart; Maris wants wind knowledge to move grain safely.","conflict":"Maris distrusts outsiders, and Veya's pride makes her bristle when Maris corrects her reading of a current.","outcome":"They agree to share knowledge, and Veya adds Maris's corridors to her chart, making it dangerous to the Cartel.","depends_on":["scn_maris_hides_grain","scn_wardens_accuse"]},{"id":"scn_kael_closes_in","title":"Ledger of Leverage","summary":"Kael's ledger-mastery reveals the weak point in the Hollow's trade: a single windmill route. He sends enforcers to seize it, and tells the Docks council that Veya's chart endangers trade.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Seize the last stable skybridge routes by cutting the Hollow's supply chain.","conflict":"His admiration for Veya's work makes him hesitate to order her chart destroyed, giving her a window to act.","outcome":"Enforcers are dispatched to the Hollow, and Kael orders Veya's copies at the Docks impounded.","depends_on":["scn_levy_at_mistral","scn_veya_meets_maris"]},{"id":"scn_enforcers_raid","title":"The Windmill Raid","summary":"Enforcers reach The Hollow just as Maris and Veya are moving grain. Using the service corridors, Maris leads Veya out but a store is lost and Veya's error in reading a wind shift nearly costs them a bridge.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Escape the raid with the grain and the chart intact.","conflict":"Veya will not admit her misreading of the wind, and Maris must choose between loyalty to home and following Veya's route.","outcome":"They escape but lose half the grain, and Maris, angry, forces Veya to admit her mistake; the chart is corrected.","depends_on":["scn_kael_closes_in"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_council","title":"The Academy Decides","summary":"At Silverspine, Veya presents the corrected chart to scholars and Wardens, and the Wardens agree to carry it to the Docks. Kael arrives with Cartel authority to claim it.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants the chart shared publicly; Kael wants it handed over under Cartel seal.","conflict":"Kael argues that open charts will cause panic and collapse of trade, while Veya's old habit of hoarding truths makes her first impulse to hide it.","outcome":"Veya, having been corrected by Maris, chooses to copy and share the chart, and Kael leaves furious, resolved to confront her at the Docks.","depends_on":["scn_enforcers_raid"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Charter","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_docks_assembly","title":"Assembly at Mistral Docks","summary":"At the Docks, the isles' delegates gather. Veya, Maris and the Wardens present the shared chart and the grain levy's costs, demanding representation in trade law. Kael faces them with the Cartel Charter.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya and Maris seek representation for the isles in trade law; Kael seeks to uphold the Charter and the Cartel's hold on the last stable routes.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery picks apart the isles' coalition, while Maris must reveal her smuggling routes to prove the levy's harm, risking her people's safety.","outcome":"Maris reveals the routes, Veya's open chart proves the Cartel's monopoly cannot survive the collapse, and Kael sees that control would cost more than it gains.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_council"]},{"id":"scn_kaels_choice","title":"Kael's Reckoning","summary":"Alone with Veya after the assembly, Kael weighs the cost of enforcing the Charter against the open chart that now belongs to everyone.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Kael must decide whether to enforce the Charter or yield; Veya wants him to support shared routes.","conflict":"Kael equates price with worth and struggles to value what cannot be sold; Veya's pride makes her gloat before she offers him a place in the new arrangement.","outcome":"Kael yields the Charter's exclusive tolls and agrees to a council with isle representation.","depends_on":["scn_docks_assembly"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"A New Charter","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hollow_harvest","title":"Grain Without Levy","summary":"In The Hollow, the levy is lifted and Maris, no longer forced to hide, opens the silos to the council's inspectors. She chooses to keep one corridor secret as insurance.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris","chr_veya"],"goal":"Maris wants The Hollow fed and secure; Veya wants to thank her and map the corridors with consent.","conflict":"Maris still trusts slowly and hesitates to share the final corridor even with Veya.","outcome":"Maris shares most routes and understands that hiding can be as brave as standing still, while Veya accepts the limits of what she may ask.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_choice"]},{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"Cables Restored","summary":"At Emberroost, Wardens and Cartel toll-masters, including Kael, jointly braid new cloudstone cables, with Kael opening his ledgers to resolve the sabotage accusation.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_veya"],"goal":"Restore the bridges using shared supplies and settle the sabotage accusation.","conflict":"Wardens distrust Kael, and Kael must expose the Cartel's own ledger entries to prove his honesty.","outcome":"The ledgers show supplies were diverted by Cartel policy, Kael accepts responsibility, and the first repaired bridge is crossed under the new council's authority.","depends_on":["scn_kaels_choice"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_new_charter","title":"The New Charter","summary":"At Silverspine, the council signs a revised charter with isle representation, and Veya publishes the full chart in the Academy, crediting her late mentor, Maris and Kael.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Formalise shared trade law and publish the chart openly.","conflict":"Veya must credit others and forgo sole recognition, while Kael and Maris still carry wariness toward each other.","outcome":"The charter is signed, Veya learns that truths are safer shared, and the isles face the drift together under a common law.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_harvest","scn_emberroost_cables"]}]}]}
</Output>
