{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","title":"The Cartographer's Mark","logline":"When Veya, a stubborn cartographer, charts a safe route through the failing skybridges, she must outmaneuver the Drift Cartel toll-master Kael, who wants her charts buried so the Cartel can seize the last stable routes before the bridges collapse.","theme":"Truths shared are safer than truths hoarded.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Fading Lines","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silverspine_survey","title":"The Shifting Charts","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya finishes a survey showing the skybridges are failing faster than anyone admits. Her wind-sight confirms her late mentor's theory that the isles are drifting apart. An old archivist reminds her of the prophecy that a chosen one will repair the bridges, and Veya scoffs at it.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Complete a survey of the failing skybridges and confirm her mentor's theory.","conflict":"The data is alarming, and Veya's stubbornness makes her reject the prophecy and any help that comes with it.","outcome":"Veya confirms the isles are drifting apart and resolves to chart a safe route, keeping her findings to herself."},{"id":"scn_docks_toll","title":"A Price on Every Crossing","summary":"At Mistral Docks, Kael tightens the toll on the remaining stable bridges and learns that Veya's charts exist. Charming and pragmatic, he sends word inviting her to share them, while privately planning to control them.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael"],"goal":"Secure the Cartel's hold on the last stable routes by raising tolls and tracking down Veya's charts.","conflict":"The Bridge Wardens accuse him of sabotaging forge-island supplies, and merchants resent the tolls.","outcome":"Kael learns what Veya has found and resolves to obtain or bury the charts.","depends_on":["scn_silverspine_survey"]},{"id":"scn_kael_offer","title":"The Rival's Offer","summary":"Kael arrives at Silverspine and offers Veya Cartel funding in exchange for exclusive rights to her charts. Their shared apprenticeship surfaces old admiration and old grievances. Veya refuses, stung by how close his offer comes to her own hunger for recognition.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Kael wants to buy the charts, and Veya wants to keep control of them.","conflict":"Veya fears becoming like the Cartel leaders, and Kael admires her skill even as he cannot let her succeed.","outcome":"Veya refuses and Kael leaves with a veiled threat, so the Cartel now treats the charts as a target.","depends_on":["scn_docks_toll"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Breaking Bridges","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_cables","title":"The Braided Cables","summary":"Veya travels to Emberroost to verify the cable failures she charted. The forge-island is short of cloudstone, and the Wardens suspect Cartel sabotage. Veya's data matches the failing bridges, but she hides how bad the pattern is because she cannot admit that her first route estimate was wrong.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya"],"goal":"Verify that her chart predictions match the failing cables.","conflict":"Her flaw makes her conceal an error in her estimate, and a Warden notices her hesitation.","outcome":"Veya learns one of her predicted safe routes is unreliable, and she keeps this secret.","depends_on":["scn_kael_offer"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_meeting","title":"Secret Paths","summary":"Veya reaches The Hollow, where Maris, who is smuggling grain around the Cartel's levy, agrees to trade her unmapped service corridors for Veya's wind-current knowledge. Maris is wary and slow to trust, but she shows Veya a corridor that avoids the broken bridges.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants an alternative route, and Maris wants to keep The Hollow fed despite the grain levy.","conflict":"Maris trusts slowly, and Veya is reluctant to share her charts in full.","outcome":"They form an alliance and a partial route is mapped, but Cartel enforcers are seen nearby.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables"]},{"id":"scn_enforcer_chase","title":"Cartel at the Silos","summary":"Kael's enforcers, acting on his orders, close in on Maris's smuggling routes. Maris uses her pathfinding to lead them away while Veya reads the wind to guide a grain skiff through the corridors. Veya's wind-debt from the crossing grows heavy.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris","chr_kael"],"goal":"Maris and Veya want to get the grain out unseen, and Kael wants to seize the shipment and learn the route.","conflict":"Kael's ledger-mastery spots the weak point in their plan, and Maris's loyalty to home pulls against her friendship with Veya.","outcome":"The grain escapes, but Kael now knows the hidden corridors exist and Veya's route data is exposed in part.","depends_on":["scn_hollow_meeting"]},{"id":"scn_docks_confrontation","title":"Ledgers and Lies","summary":"Veya goes to Mistral Docks to prove the Cartel is hoarding the stable routes. Kael exposes her concealed error and uses it to discredit her in front of the merchants. Veya, who cannot admit fault, argues back and loses the room.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael"],"goal":"Veya wants to expose Cartel hoarding, and Kael wants to discredit her charts.","conflict":"Veya's flaw leaves her unable to concede her mistake, which hands Kael the advantage.","outcome":"Her charts are publicly doubted and the Cartel closes more routes, leaving Veya isolated.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_cables","scn_enforcer_chase"]},{"id":"scn_maris_choice","title":"The Cost of Hiding","summary":"Maris, ready to give up on the friendship, finds Veya alone at The Hollow. Veya finally admits her error and offers to share every chart openly. Maris, who rarely forgives, chooses to trust her and opens the last secret corridors.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to repair the trust she damaged, and Maris wants to decide whether to risk her isle's secrets.","conflict":"Maris's slow trust and Veya's pride clash until Veya concedes.","outcome":"Veya admits her error and Maris shares the corridors, leaving them with a complete route and a plan to broadcast it.","depends_on":["scn_docks_confrontation"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Bridge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_emberroost_gambit","title":"Charts for All","summary":"Veya brings copies of her corrected charts to Emberroost, where the Wardens help her distribute them. Kael arrives with enforcers to seize the last stable routes. Veya's wind-sight spots a failing cable and warns that his seizure will overload the final bridge.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to release the charts publicly, and Kael wants to seize the final stable routes.","conflict":"Kael's seizure would overload the last bridge, and he must choose between control and the warning of a rival he respects.","outcome":"The cable begins to fail and both rivals realise the route can only hold if the charts are shared.","depends_on":["scn_maris_choice"]},{"id":"scn_bridge_crossing","title":"The Prophecy Crossing","summary":"As the bridge gives way, Veya reads the winds and calls out the safe path while Maris guides the crowd through the service corridors and Kael, finally acting on Veya's chart, orders his enforcers to hold the cables. In the crossing the old prophecy seems to come true, though it is the shared work of many hands.","location_id":"loc_emberroost","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Get everyone across the failing bridge safely using Veya's route.","conflict":"The bridge collapses faster than predicted, and Kael must give up control of his enforcers and his ledgers to save the crossing.","outcome":"The crowd crosses and the bridge is stabilised, with Kael's help and Veya's charts proving the decisive factors.","depends_on":["scn_emberroost_gambit"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"A Shared Map","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_kael_reckoning","title":"The Price of Control","summary":"Back at Mistral Docks, the merchants confront Kael over the rushed tolls and the sabotage claims. Kael, who has seen that control costs more than it gains, concedes the levy and opens the routes, accepting the wind-debt he owes in labour.","location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","character_ids":["chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Kael wants to repair the Cartel's standing, and Maris wants the grain levy lifted.","conflict":"Kael's pride and his belief that price equals worth resist giving up control.","outcome":"Kael lifts the grain levy and opens the routes, and the Cartel's monopoly ends.","depends_on":["scn_bridge_crossing"]},{"id":"scn_hollow_return","title":"Grain for Every Isle","summary":"Maris returns to The Hollow as the first open grain shipments leave, finding that hiding and standing still have both kept her isle alive. She and the Hollow Circle plan shared shipping with the Wardens.","location_id":"loc_the_hollow","character_ids":["chr_maris"],"goal":"Restore open grain trade now that the levy is lifted.","conflict":"The Hollow Circle is still wary of Cartel promises and slow to trust the new arrangement.","outcome":"The Hollow resumes open trade and Maris accepts that her quiet courage mattered.","depends_on":["scn_kael_reckoning"]},{"id":"scn_silverspine_atlas","title":"The Cartographer's Mark","summary":"At Silverspine Academy, Veya adds her mark to a shared atlas of the skybridge network, open to every isle and credited to her mentor's theory. She tells the archivist the prophecy was never about one chosen person, and Kael and Maris stand among those who now help to repair the bridges.","location_id":"loc_silverspine","character_ids":["chr_veya","chr_kael","chr_maris"],"goal":"Veya wants to publish the atlas openly and honour her mentor's theory.","conflict":"Veya's craving for recognition tempts her to keep sole credit until she chooses to share it.","outcome":"The atlas is published for all isles and the bridges begin to be repaired together.","depends_on":["scn_kael_reckoning","scn_hollow_return"]}]}]}
