{"world_id":"wld_sparrow","title":"The Empty Isle","logline":"Elara, the lone engineer of a research dome on a frozen moon, races to repair the single irreparable battery that keeps the Habitation Bay alive, and must decide whether to keep fighting entropy or face its certainty before the last of the power fails.","theme":"Letting go can be the last act of survival","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Dying Hum","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_dying_hum","title":"The Dying Hum","summary":"Elara wakes in the Habitation Bay and hears a wrongness in the power grid's pitch. Reading the telemetry by ear, she realises the battery's decline is accelerating.","location_id":"loc_bay","character_ids":["chr_elara"],"goal":"Confirm the true state of the battery using her ear for the grid's telemetry.","conflict":"The readings are ambiguous and she is alone, with no second opinion and no outside contact.","outcome":"She confirms the battery is failing faster than expected and resolves to repair it, dismissing the idea that it is beyond saving."},{"id":"scn_rationing_plan","title":"The Rationing Plan","summary":"Elara methodically sorts the bay's systems, deciding which to shut down to stretch the battery's remaining charge while she works on a fix.","location_id":"loc_bay","character_ids":["chr_elara"],"goal":"Cut power consumption enough to buy time for a repair.","conflict":"Every system she shuts down makes the bay colder and more hostile, and her stubbornness makes her reject cuts that would give a real margin.","outcome":"She achieves a modest saving but leaves heating higher than is safe, setting up a faster drain later.","depends_on":["scn_dying_hum"]}]},{"id":"act_rising","title":"Entropy Pushes Back","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_first_repair","title":"The First Repair Attempt","summary":"Elara opens the battery housing and tries to rebalance its failing cells, drawing on her diagnostic skill to find the weakest ones.","location_id":"loc_bay","character_ids":["chr_elara"],"goal":"Repair the failing battery before it dies.","conflict":"The world's rule is absolute: a depleted battery cannot be repaired, so any mistake costs charge she cannot recover.","outcome":"The attempt briefly stabilises output but permanently burns a chunk of reserve charge.","depends_on":["scn_rationing_plan"]},{"id":"scn_cold_creeps","title":"The Cold Creeps In","summary":"The reserve she burned forces emergency load shedding. The bay's temperature falls and Elara, methodical to a fault, logs every degree while refusing to abandon the repair.","location_id":"loc_bay","character_ids":["chr_elara"],"goal":"Keep the bay habitable long enough for rescue.","conflict":"Her compassion for the dome's dying systems and her stubbornness keep her from sacrificing them, so the cold spreads.","outcome":"She is forced to shrink her living space within the bay and abandon part of the dome's equipment.","depends_on":["scn_first_repair"]},{"id":"scn_second_failure","title":"The Second Failure","summary":"A more aggressive repair, made against her own diagnostics, collapses a group of cells and the grid's hum drops to a faltering tone.","location_id":"loc_bay","character_ids":["chr_elara"],"goal":"Force the battery back to full capacity with a bolder fix.","conflict":"Her flaw drives her to ignore telemetry that says the battery cannot be saved, even as she hears the proof by ear.","outcome":"The battery loses most of its remaining life, and Elara can no longer deny how little time is left.","depends_on":["scn_cold_creeps"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Last Charge","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_hope_vs_entropy","title":"Hope Versus Entropy","summary":"With the battery near its end, Elara faces the confrontation she has been avoiding: the certainty that it cannot be saved against her hope that it can.","location_id":"loc_bay","character_ids":["chr_elara"],"goal":"Decide whether to attempt one final repair or to spend what remains on 